how do i get started on youtube  that's a question i came in from one of  my youtube viewers uh name is levine  holland  who wrote in to say hi everyone thank  you for your videos i'm a new financial  advisor  in toronto my hometown and would like to  get started creating good content for  youtube channel can you share how you  got started thank you  so great question for me when i'm  starting any project  related to my business if it's marketing  new project creation  services whatever it is there has to be  a founding core  reason purpose behind it so i started  doing videos  because i felt that i was a visual  learner and  i enjoyed learning from videos most of  the content that i created  was written so newsletters website  content articles that kind of stuff  and i felt that i learned better through  videos and i wanted to  do videos because i felt like it could  impact a lot more people  it suits my learning style and felt like  it could help others as well  so it wasn't i need to find a way to  market my business it wasn't i want to  be a youtube sensation  the core reason of starting this channel  was to help entrepreneurs and i felt it  was a way better  learning experience for people who are  tuning in  so you have to start with something that  you believe in and that's that's  passionate  so why are you starting this youtube  channel if it's genuine if it's going to  help people  if you're excited about it then it's  worth getting started  if it's somebody told me to start  youtube channel because it's great  marketing  you're not gonna have success with it  okay you have to start with the reason  from there any new project i start i  always start small  test it out see if it's for me see if i  can get momentum going see if i'm still  excited a couple weeks later  and then continue to invest into it i  hate spending money till i'm making  money and  with youtube there's some there's some  equipment costs  right so when i started up i just used  my regular camera  the videos sucked you can go back the  quality of the content was pretty good  but the production quality was terrible  i used my home camera no microphone  terrible lighting  had no idea what it was doing and people  still like those videos so i keep them  up on my channel even though  it's it's i feel like i should take them  down it's a little embarrassing but  people like it  and i started off small i started with  one video  and i posted it and we got some  responses and so i posted another video  and i found eventually  a way to make money doing it  because it promotes my brand promotes  what i'm talking about  and bigger companies were interested in  coming on board and sponsoring some of  them  i didn't start spending a lot of money  until i found a way to make money  and also make sure this is something i  wanted to stick with  here's the problem with a lot of  entrepreneurs we get excited about a  project we go out and we invest  a ton of our time a ton of dollars into  buying  the equipment the gear the supplies  everything we need to make this project  take off  we get into it and then it dies  you lose the excitement it's harder than  you think it was going to be it dies  and you're stuck with all this equipment  inventory supplies that now you're not  going to use  and i didn't want that to happen with my  videos i didn't want to get all excited  at the start  go out and buy a camera tripod lighting  microphone  all that gear only to then  in a couple weeks say ah you know what  this isn't for me  i'm not liking this it's not what i  thought it was gonna be and now i'm  stuck  out all this expenses so i made sure it  was for me  i got started my first camera was  uh something like my home camera wasn't  anything fancy some of the videos you'll  see are wobbly  i just put it up on my my dresser and  i filmed myself so that they weren't  great by any means  and as i learned more about it as i  started making a little bit of money off  it  then i invested into better cameras i  went through four different cameras all  through costco because it had a 90 day  return policy  where most video stores would be like 7  or 14 days  and i kept upgrading my camera because i  needed more things you know i needed to  have an external microphone jack so i  could plug in a microphone  where most cameras you know the base  models don't have it  so i kept upgrading and eventually i  stuck with what i'm using now it's a  sony camcorder it's got the external mic  i use the sony  uh microphone i have uh  the stand the tripod for the video  camera that stands on i usually  read off questions that come from  readers on my phone  and at the start i did everything myself  editing the videos producing the videos  putting up on youtube  eventually i hired somebody so now i  record all my videos put them in dropbox  and uh christina who's on my team  hey christina she's watching this video  now she's editing  uh she'll put on the intro put the music  put the effects  closing post it to my youtube channel  schedule it all that stuff so it takes  it out of my hands and freezes up my  time to do it  it started small and it built up to  become  core of what i do i'm doing 14 videos a  week now  my wednesdays are basically video days  it's wednesday  afternoon here and i'm recording my  videos it's become  core to what i do a lot of the projects  that we start up don't end up going  anywhere  but a few of them stick and become  really important and part of your  messaging part of your brain and part of  what you do  on a regular basis so it's worth  spending the time investing into it  and money when you know that this is  something that's going to be really  important to what you're going to do  most of the content that i talk about  are things that i care about  so it'll be questions that come in from  readers  just like you how did i get started on  youtube how can i you know make it  bigger  i answer questions i'll share my own  thoughts if i'm modeling a successful  entrepreneur or something that happened  to me during the week  i experiment with some raw footage of  things of me doing something or a rant  that i have  you want to make sure that each video  that you have has a message  what should people care about right it's  not just you sitting there eating  pancakes  you have something that is meaningful  that you want to share with people  that's going to touch their lives  for the few minutes that they're  spending watching your video now the  first few days you make will probably  suck you'll be nervous  it takes a lot of practice to get used  to talk in front of the camera  i had dozens of takes for each video  that came out  at the beginning now most of them is is  one shot  make the video if there's a mistake  usually just keep going through  it takes a while to get used to it to  get good at it  and and you're always going to be your  own worst critic you're going to look  back and say oh man that sucked  but you know put it up see what happens  and continue making them better  each time so that's how i got started on  youtube  and again if you're doing it for the  right reasons and you start small and  you're sharing a passionate message  then you're going to have success with  it too believe for those of you watching  you like the video please give it a  thumbs up below  makes me want to do more for you and i'd  love to hear what you got to think about  this video if you've had success on  youtube  or if you have a different question for  your business please leave it in the  comments below and i'll make a video  reply for you  thank you guys see you soon  you
 

